==English==

===Verb===
'''moonlighting'''

# {{present participle of|[[moonlight#Verb|moonlight]]}}  To take a job, to supplement one's daytime earnings.  This is normally considered a shady situation.

For example, an employee of 'ABC Plumbing' works during the day doing service calls for his boss.  At one of those service calls, the home owner asks the employee if they can 'come back at night' or another time to do the job at a cheaper rate (usually for cash).  The worker agrees and completes the task at night (or on a weekend so no one knows about it).  That is called Moonlighting.  
